      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name}: In advance, I don't understand technically how IK works so apologies if I'm asking for the obvious or something stupid. \nIs there a way to lower the overall stiffness between bones in the central bone chain? Or equivelantly, split up \"excess\" angles either equally or in a ratio amongst all bones in the chain?\nAs it stands the central bone chain in question remains incredibly stiff, giving the appearance of a ramrod straight back in most situations and so excess angles are being absorbed in the shortext bone, the neck (see pic). If the stiffness was lowered throughout the hip->head chain there should be enough degrees of freedom that deformations look more natural.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
