      "value": "@{5e44a1bd0c91c2477a8b8acb|full_name}: In my experience placing the hip tracker anywhere on front-center is a big no-no - the belly is soft and the tracker is free to rotate and shift quite a lot. Placing it on the side or the back, where it's mostly supported by the hip bone, usually provides more stable tracking.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
